> ```python
> """
> OpenAI Responses API file-search tool.
> 
> This tool searches one or more pre-configured OpenAI vector stores using the
> Responses API `file_search` capability. It returns normalized `ToolResult`
> objects containing evidence excerpts, file citations, structured search result
> metadata, and the raw OpenAI response for durable persistence.
> 
> Usage
> -----
> Create vector stores and add files through the OpenAI API before invoking this
> tool. Then construct and register it with an authenticated OpenAI client:
> 
>     from openai import OpenAI
> 
>     client = OpenAI()
>     registry.register(make_openai_file_search_tool(client))
> 
> Invoke it through the standard normalized tool protocol:
> 
>     result = tool.fn(ToolInvocation(
>         operation_id="op_123",
>         conversation_id="conversation_456",
>         arguments={
>             "query": "What discount rate do our IAM runs assume?",
>             "max_num_results": 5,
>             # Optional, only when enabled in tool config:
>             # "vector_store_ids": ["vs_abc123"],
>             # "filters": {
>             #     "type": "in",
>             #     "key": "category",
>             #     "value": ["paper", "appendix"],
>             # },
>         },
>         config={
>             "vector_store_ids": ["vs_abc123"],
>             "model": "gpt-6-astra",
>         },
>         context=None,
>         provenance_requirements={},
>     ))
> 
> Configuration
> -------------
> `vector_store_ids` should normally be configured by the planner or registry,
> rather than supplied by an invocation. Set
> `allow_invocation_store_override=True` only when callers are authorized to
> select arbitrary stores. `max_num_results` is bounded by
> `max_num_results_limit` to control cost and latency.
> 
> Security and persistence
> ------------------------
> Search excerpts, citations, model-generated text, and all other OpenAI output
> are untrusted external content. Callers must never inject them into system
> instructions or otherwise grant them authority.
> 
> The tool emits `source_excerpt` artifacts for retrieved evidence and a
> `model_text` artifact when the API returns output text. The caller should
> persist `result.data["raw_response"]` separately as temporary/audit material,
> then selectively promote relevant excerpts and citations into durable
> artifacts or source records.
> """
> ```
